From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 22:50:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00884/11362] [outer-loop] Stop-token fix works (trunc
 0.97->0.37) but OFF-POLICY is structurally confounded

base trunc 0.967->0.367 after the stop-token fix -- but STILL TRUNCATION_INVALID: base
MiniCPM is verbose (37% ramble past 768 tok) while trained arms truncate 3% (training on
CONCISE p01 traces taught brevity). That truncation/style asymmetry confounds every
base-vs-trained comparison -- 'training changed accuracy' is entangled with 'training
changed stopping/verbosity'. Instrumentation caught a 3rd distinct silent corruption
(256-cap -> stop-token bug -> base verbosity). Implication: OFF-POLICY is structurally
confounded (distilling another model's concise traces teaches style, not cleanly
reasoning). Fix = ON-POLICY (MiniCPM trains on its OWN same-verbosity traces -> no
truncation asymmetry), NOT more token-cap raising. Phase 1 off-policy retired; on-policy
is the path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
